---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "Privacy Policy — Code to Click";
const description = "How Code to Click collects, uses and protects your information, and the choices you have — including our use of cookies.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
<section class="phero">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-bottom:52px">
    <div class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</div>
    <span class="eyebrow kick">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy <span class="g">Policy</span></h1>
    <div class="meta" style="color:#8FA0C4;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono';font-size:12px;margin-top:16px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap"><span>Last updated: 21 August 2026</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article prose reveal">
      <p class="lead">This Privacy Policy explains how Code to Click (&ldquo;Code to Click&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;) collects, uses and safeguards information when you visit codetoclick.ai or contact us. We keep this deliberately simple: we collect only what we need to respond to you and to run our website well.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Code to Click is a Salesforce-first, AI-native consulting company. For any question about this policy or your data, you can reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@codetoclick.ai">hello@codetoclick.ai</a>.</p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect information in two ways:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you complete our contact form or email us, we collect the details you choose to share &mdash; typically your name, work email, company, and the content of your message.</li>
        <li><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting and analytics tools may record technical data such as your browser type, device, approximate region and the pages you view. This helps us keep the site secure and understand what&rsquo;s useful.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use your information</h2>
      <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>respond to your enquiry and follow up about working together;</li>
        <li>provide, maintain, secure and improve our website;</li>
        <li>protect against spam, fraud and abuse; and</li>
        <li>meet legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information, and we don&rsquo;t share it with third parties for their own marketing.</p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Cookies &amp; similar technologies</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device. We use a small number of them:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> keep the site working and remember your cookie choice. These are always on because the site relies on them.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> help us understand how the site is used, in aggregate, so we can improve it. These are only set with your consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>When you first visit, we show a consent banner so you can accept or decline non-essential cookies. You can change your mind at any time by clearing this site&rsquo;s cookies in your browser, which will bring the banner back. Most browsers also let you block or delete cookies through their settings.</p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>We rely on a few trusted providers to run our site and communicate with you &mdash; for example our website host and content delivery network, our email provider, and our form-handling service. These providers process data only on our instructions and under their own security and privacy commitments.</p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>We keep enquiry details for as long as needed to respond and to maintain a record of our correspondence, and then delete or anonymise them. Technical and analytics data is retained for a limited period consistent with keeping the site secure and useful.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or restrict the use of your personal information, to object to certain processing, and to withdraw consent. To exercise any of these, email us at <a href="mailto:hello@codetoclick.ai">hello@codetoclick.ai</a> and we&rsquo;ll respond within a reasonable time.</p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>We use appropriate technical and organizational measures &mdash; including least-privilege access and secure environments &mdash; to protect your information. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, but we work to keep your data safe and to limit what we collect in the first place.</p>

      <h2>Children&rsquo;s privacy</h2>
      <p>Our website is intended for businesses and professionals. It is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 16.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we&rsquo;ll revise the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date above, and significant changes will be reflected here.</p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy or this policy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@codetoclick.ai">hello@codetoclick.ai</a> &mdash; a real person will get back to you.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="blk alt" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px"><div class="wrap"><div class="ctaband reveal">
  <h2>Have a project in mind?</h2>
  <p>Tell us what you&rsquo;re building &mdash; we reply within one business day.</p>
  <div class="cta"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Book a consult &rarr;</a></div>
</div></div></section>
</Base>
